<title>USA: GE gets EVA airways order valued at $750 mln.</title>
<headline>GE gets EVA airways order valued at $750 mln.</headline>
<dateline>EVENDALE, OHIO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co said its aircraft engine unit received an order valued at $750 million from Taiwan's EVA Airways Corp for 82 GE CF6-80 series turbofan engines.</p>
<p>GE did not say how much the order would add to its earnings.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to begin delivering the aircraft in 1997.</p>
<p>EVA already has 26 aircraft powered by CF6-8032 engines, GE said.</p>
</text>
